1
00:00:04,770 --> 00:00:05,550
莱纳德
Leonard...

2
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:07,360
我有个天大的坏消息
I've got terrible news.

3
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:08,800
怎么了
What's going on?

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,390
在我说之前  或许需要给你点心里缓冲
Before I tell you, perhaps I should soften the blow.

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:15,950
你的脸对称得很讨喜
You're face is pleasingly symmetrical.

6
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:18,740
你就说吧
Just tell me.

7
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:20,570
一个瑞典的物理学家团队
A Swedish team of physicists

8
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:24,020
想要抢先一步进行我们的超流体漩涡实验
is trying to scoop our super-fluid vortex experiment.

9
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:25,890
好吧  这是有点恶心
Oh, well, that kind of stinks.

10
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:27,650
什么叫"有点恶心"
"That kind of stinks"?

11
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,230
你应该要更不爽啊
Why aren't you more upset?

12
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:30,930
我刚才给你缓冲太多了吗
Did I soften the blow too much?

13
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:35,160
因为这副尊容更像是一幅毕加索的抽象画
Because this here is more like a Picasso painting.

14
00:00:36,310 --> 00:00:37,470
那我们要怎么办
What are we going to do?

15
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:39,040
立刻进行实验
Perform the experiment immediately.

16
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:41,640
我也想  但我们需要液氦
I'd love to, but we need liquid helium

17
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:43,740
而我们订的氦要晚一个月才到
and our shipment's on back order for a month.

18
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:45,890
什么  一个月  你跟我闹呢
A month? What? Are you kidding me?

19
00:00:45,890 --> 00:00:48,540
现在就很适合你给我做心里缓冲啊
That would have been a good time for you to soften the blow.

20
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,930
这T恤能衬托出你那深邃的蓝眸
That shirt brings out the blue in your eyes.

21
00:00:52,310 --> 00:00:54,670
谢谢  你嘴真甜
Thank you. Aren't you sweet.

22
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,180
我们去查查大学里
Let's go check to see if the university

23
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:58,880
还有没有氦气存货吧
has any helium in reserve.

24
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:01,630
你知道我今天差点就不穿这件衣服吗
Did you know that I almost didn't wear this shirt today?

25
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:05,060
巴里  我们碰到了麻烦
Hey, Barry, we're in trouble.

26
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:06,270
我们需要液氦
We need liquid helium--

27
00:01:06,270 --> 00:01:07,830
系里有多余的可以让我们用吗
does the department have any we can use?

28
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:09,070
抱歉  这东西有些短缺
Sorry, there's a shortage.

29
00:01:09,070 --> 00:01:12,160
而仅有的存货  我要拿来做量子激发研究
And what we do have I need for my quantum excitation study.

30
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:14,250
你那个实验不需要用多少啊
But you won't need much for that.

31
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:15,540
的确  但如果成功了
True, but if it's successful,

32
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:17,670
我开派对要拿来灌气球啊
I'm having a party with balloons.

33
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:20,460
别这样  巴里  有个瑞典团队
Come on, Barry, there's a Swedish team

34
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:21,980
想抢先进行我们的实验
trying to run our experiment before us.

35
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:23,300
你真不能匀一点给我们吗
Can't you spare any?

36
00:01:23,630 --> 00:01:26,130
你们老实说  如果今天换我碰到这情况
Be honest-- if the shoe was on the other foot,

37
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:27,790
你们会愿意帮我吗
would you do this for me?

38
00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:29,750
-会  -不可能
- Yes. - No chance.

39
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:31,510
你帮倒忙呢
What are you doing?

40
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:33,610
他说老实说  所以我老实说啊
He said be honest, so I was honest.

41
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:36,800
你母亲没教你吗  诚实为上
Didn't your mother tell you? It's the best policy.

42
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:37,990
所以你意下如何
So, what do you say?

43
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:39,330
下辈子吧
Hell no.

44
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:43,770
他可以给我们点缓冲再说的
He could've softened the blow.

45
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,350
生

46
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,350
活

47
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,350
大

48
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,350
爆

49
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,350
炸

50
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,350
第九季  第六集

51
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:12,230
你们为啥需要找他要氦气
Why do you need Kripke?

52
00:02:12,230 --> 00:02:14,560
你们不能直接去派对用品店买点吗
Can't you just go to Party City for helium?

53
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:17,530
我们得跑遍它们全加州的店才够
We'd have to go to every Party City in California.

54
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:21,650
听起来就像5月5日节时的你啊
Sounds like you on Cinco de Mayo.

55
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:21,650
墨西哥节日  庆祝某场战役的胜利
在节日当日会有各种派对  舞蹈等等

56
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:24,350
我办的那个派对到5月7日
Hey, people were still talking about that party

57
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:27,370
还有人赞不绝口呢
on siete de Mayo.

58
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,500
莱纳德  如果那个瑞典团队赢了我们
Leonard, if that Swedish team beats us,

59
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:32,600
我此生都再也不愿享用那个国家的东西了
I will never be able to enjoy anything from their country again.

60
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,860
那真挺可惜的  因为瑞典的肉丸
Which is a shame, because Swedish meatballs

61
